{
  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our current best is config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) at 0.527 acc, which modestly beats RNA-only (0.485) by ~4%. Image alone (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality contributes limited signal with a standard CNN. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether the image encoder is the bottleneck limiting the multimodal gain, or whether the image modality is fundamentally weak for this task. This experiment tests whether upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L (config_022) meaningfully improves the multimodal setup, while keeping all other settings identical to config_016 (pca_n2000, singleprofile, concat fusion). This is a clean single-variable comparison. If ViT-L yields a substantial improvement, it validates investing remaining budget in stronger multimodal variants (multiprofile, transformer aggregation). If it does not, it indicates the image modality is inherently limited here, and we should pivot remaining experiments toward improving the RNA representation (scgpt, scvi) or multiprofile aggregation in the RNA-only or multimodal setting."
}

